   "entity": "code-quantumn",
   "url": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
   "canonical_url": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai",
   "title": "Stop guessing auto scaling targets for TTS on Amazon SageMaker AI",
   "snippet": "Teams deploying custom text-to-speech models on Amazon SageMaker AI often guess at autoscaling thresholds, and a wrong guess either wastes GPU spend or breaches a latency SLO. This post deploys Kokoro-82M as a custom container and derives a measured autoscaling policy from two live-endpoint measurements, Q_max and T_total, instead of guesswork.",
